## 4. The contract (A1)

9 schemas under packages/contracts/schemas/, each JSON Schema 2020-12 with a versioned $id
`https://project-air.dev/contracts/0.1.0/<entity>.schema.json`:

    account.schema.json        Account (id, email, displayName, locale enum de/en, timestamps)
    workspace.schema.json      Workspace (id, name, ownerId, timestamps)
    board.schema.json          Board (id, workspaceId, ownerId, title, visibility enum, archived)
    note.schema.json           Note (id, workspaceId, title, timestamps; AD-4, body later)
    card.schema.json           Note card placement (boardId, noteId, zoneId?, x, y, w, h, z)
    zone.schema.json           Zone (boardId, title, x, y, w, h, z; no nested zones)
    block.schema.json          Block (type enum checklist/palette/columns/timeline/table,
                               if/then minimum size per type)
    edge.schema.json           Edge (boardId, from/to = {kind:"card", id}; cards only)
    board-content.schema.json  Root document ($refs to every entity, contractVersion const 0.1.0)

Encoded rules: UUIDv7 id pattern, ISO-8601 timestamps with timezone, fractional index `z` as a
string, numeric minimum sizes (note card 176x80, zone 256x192, checklist/palette 224x128, columns
368x192, timeline 320x160, table 288x160), required fields, fixed enums, `additionalProperties:
false` everywhere. The tests assert each of these values and that every schema has a versioned
$id and required fields.

## 5. Fixtures (A2)

35 fixtures under packages/contracts/fixtures/<entity>/ in the wrapper `{schema, valid, reason,
data}`; every schema has at least one valid and one invalid example:
account 4, workspace 2, board 3, note 2, card 4, zone 3, block 11 (one valid and one below-minimum
invalid per block type plus an unknown type), edge 3, board-content 3. Every invalid fixture names
the violated rule in `reason` (minimum size, required field, enum, nesting, edge endpoint, version).

The test suite validates all fixtures against the schemas with a small built-in structural
validator for the keywords used (type, required, properties, additionalProperties, enum, const,
pattern, minLength, maxLength, minimum, items, allOf/if/then, $ref): all valid fixtures pass, all
invalid fixtures fail. The root valid fixture is cross-checked for AD-4 (notes exist once and cards
reference them), the parent relation (board -> zone -> card, zones not nested) and card-only edge
endpoints.

